         "step": 1,
         "text": "Complete the square in the quadratic: \\( x^{2} + 4 x + 29 = \\left(x + 2\\right)^{2} + 25 \\).",
         "rule_named": "completing the square"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The integrand has the shape of an inverse trigonometric derivative, \\( \\frac{d}{dx} \\arctan\\left(\\frac{x + 2}{5}\\right) = \\frac{5}{25 + \\left(x + 2\\right)^{2}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "antiderivative read from a derivative rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "With \\( u = \\frac{x + 2}{5}, \\; dx = 5\\,du \\), the integral becomes \\( \\int \\frac{12}{25\\left(1 + u^{2}\\right)} \\cdot 5\\,du = \\frac{12}{5} \\int \\frac{du}{1 + u^{2}} \\), which is \\( \\frac{12 \\arctan{\\left(\\frac{x}{5} + \\frac{2}{5} \\right)}}{5} + C \\).",
